s/uvalde-county"],["ARC or PLC in Uvalde County","/arc-plc/texas/uvalde-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 12 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and September to October came in under 90% of normal in 42 of those 75 years. In 2025, November to December came in at 19% of normal on the middle of the grids. So far in 2026, June to July came in at 258% of normal there. Every grid had its driest year in 1956, and grid 10920 came in at 35% of normal that year.</p>"}
